# A record named as a value, `first(as: Session)`, names the record of the
# module it is written in (kexhq/kex#539). Once Net.HTTP.WebSocket — which
# declares its own `record Session` — was part of the program, BEAM passed
# the bare atom 'Session', which the run-time registry could no longer tell
# apart ("Not a record type: Atom"), and the walker preferred the imported
# WebSocket record over the module's own ("Unknown field").

using Net.HTTP.WebSocket

main do
  IO.printLine(RecordValue.Sessions.holder)
  IO.printLine(Net.HTTP.WebSocket.Session { subprotocol: Just("chat") }.subprotocol)
end
